Article 2 (Persons Authorized to Issue Orders upon Request)
(1) Where an urgent military necessity exists and a commander of the military police or the commander of a military police battalion (or, where unavoidable circumstances exist, such as an interruption of transportation or communications, the commander of a military police company) makes a request, any of the following commanders may temporarily require enlisted personnel of the various branches of service to assist in military police duties: [Amended on February 4, 2020.]
1. Army commander;
2. Division commander;
3. Formation commander (byeongdan commander);
4. Fortress commander;
5. Garrison commander;
6. Control command commander;
7. Security command commander.
(2) Where enlisted personnel have been required to assist in military police duties under paragraph (1), ratification by the Chief of Staff of the relevant armed service shall be obtained without delay. [Amended on February 4, 2020.]
